  "notes": [
    "Reflexive form of *ir* (to go). Completely irregular — one of the most irregular verbs in Spanish.",
    "Presente: entirely suppletive (*voy, vas, va, vamos, van*) — shares forms with *ir*.",
    "Pretérito Indefinido: also suppletive, same forms as *ser* (*fui, fuiste, fue, fuimos, fueron*).",
    "Pretérito Imperfecto: *iba, ibas, iba, íbamos, iban* — accent on nosotros form only.",
    "Past participle: ***ido***.",
    "Reflexive pronouns (me/te/se/nos/se) always precede the conjugated verb.",
    "*¡Me voy!* (I'm leaving!)",
    "*Se fue sin decir adiós.* (He left without saying goodbye.)",
    "*¿A qué hora te vas mañana?* (What time are you leaving tomorrow?)",
    "*Se nos fue la luz.* (The power went out on us.)",
    "Related: *ir* (to go — non-reflexive), *la ida* (outward journey), *de ida y vuelta* (return/round trip)"
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/i/Irse.md"
